## Validation Patterns

### Input Validation
```typescript
const handleProcess = async () => {
  if (isProcessing) return

  if (!userPrompt.trim()) {
    toast({
      title: 'Error',
      description: 'Please describe what you would like to analyze',
      variant: 'destructive'
    })
    return
  }

  // Continue with processing...
}
```

### Token Validation
```typescript
// Check token requirements before starting
if (onBeforeStart) {
  try {
    const canProceed = await onBeforeStart()
    if (!canProceed) {
      return
    }
  } catch (error) {
    toast({
      title: 'Error',
      description: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to validate requirements',
      variant: 'destructive'
    })
    return
  }
}
```

## Error Recovery Patterns

### Retry Mechanisms
```typescript
const handleRetry = () => {
  processingState.clearState()
  processingState.startProcessing({
    userPrompt: userPrompt.trim()
  })
}

// Retry button in error state
{processingState.error && (
  <Button onClick={handleRetry} className="mt-4">
    <RefreshCw className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
    Try Again
  </Button>
)}
```

### Clear State on Error
```typescript
const handleNewAnalysis = () => {
  setGrokResult(null)
  processingState.clearState()
  setUserPrompt('')
}
```

## API Error Handling

### Fetch Error Handling
```typescript
try {
  const response = await fetch('/api/document-processing', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ userPrompt })
  })

  if (!response.ok) {
    const errorData = await response.text()
    throw new Error(`API Error: ${response.status} - ${errorData}`)
  }

  const data = await response.json()
  // Handle success...
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Processing error:', error)
  toast({
    title: 'Processing Failed',
    description: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'An unexpected error occurred',
    variant: 'destructive'
  })
}
```

### Network Error Handling
```typescript
// Handle network connectivity issues
if (error instanceof TypeError && error.message.includes('fetch')) {
  toast({
    title: 'Connection Error',
    description: 'Please check your internet connection and try again',
    variant: 'destructive'
  })
  return
}
```

## User Experience Guidelines

### Error Message Principles
1. **Be specific**: Tell users exactly what went wrong
2. **Be helpful**: Provide actionable next steps
3. **Be concise**: Keep error messages short and clear
4. **Be consistent**: Use consistent language and tone

### Error Message Examples
```typescript
// Good error messages
"No relevant documents found for your query. Try rephrasing your request or upload more documents."
"The analysis took too long to complete. Please try with a simpler request."
"Please describe what you would like to analyze"

// Bad error messages
"Error occurred"
"Something went wrong"
"Invalid input"
```

